    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Laravel MongoDB extends Laravel’s Eloquent and query-builder APIs to operate on MongoDB data. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/interact-data/query-builder.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e00bad082545a8f750fd8fb6cb6dedff54e282ba88104e563c17bd41d5df4787",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6d061e53f948664bec90bef03c9b099fae94fa5b56c24e7d58c0595adf3565fb",
            "ev:8d241262982a96cc4ab90383c0d22807fc7f7c210216093222e64c2e90e8994d"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/mongodb/laravel-mongodb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Define a MongoDB Eloquent model by extending `MongoDB\\Laravel\\Eloquent\\Model`. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/model-data/model-class.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3ac131115eaa34fa2f333db221c9a58b2c7eea9b6beab88a2a556d39cd8042e3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:79d0d1f1ab360ef2e310a3ba9f2ad6b8c09549f06b1320637dadf66b10326122",
            "ev:b07889d2fbf76d73885c56b2ba729c8d9566c96d3ad0c1cbc43d40942f319c03"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-laravel-eloquent-style-queries-with-laravel-mongodb/view"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Models use the snake-case plural class name as the default collection; override `$table` to choose another collection. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/model-data/model-class.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d4f22537f610c356d3c4558e477b47d3f072fb53870323f168985dca81cfe7c8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:c5adfb1281e530140eaa0336c4550addb4ca01101f80b9c7246587e8e3ca0062"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A MongoDB Eloquent model can use the `Illuminate\\Database\\Eloquent\\SoftDeletes` trait: deleting marks the document with `deleted_at`, and normal retrieval automatically excludes deleted documents. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/model-data/model-class.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d6e5fd5018d8ef1dda7073f19e3123063440aa0cf5c13a843f39cb161363080b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
