            "ev:541374a5e464d53f55487739faa19ab4eafcb84d9c6e92da6dfdcf933eab1987"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-laravel-eloquent-style-queries-with-laravel-mongodb/view"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The query-builder documentation says results are `stdClass` objects starting in Laravel MongoDB v5.0. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/interact-data/query-builder.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:03bf2d62c5aa3b54bc994018552a8880e3c49269f548c3080bfff71653045c7f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:cf62243c464d6816e5cfe1f6e9a7e71b7afb9bce40a2bb7692d92a7a52398a64"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The integration exposes MongoDB `_id` through the `id` alias; query-builder find results present `_id` as `id`, so separate fields with both names are incompatible with that conversion. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/model-data/model-class.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:de51d28e5bb4f7434623738d91ae3d9d462f2e7aa8601e6751ebe839905bdcab",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:15ab5fef8d6051f605dd3db3ec300702188cd0e1c89b384fb406f3cc40b6fb5b",
            "ev:446ee4a096379ec9694690f1333049509148c57f9e860ab73cd17af1e27a35b0"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/interact-data/query-builder.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Laravel MongoDB supports explicit transaction control with `DB::beginTransaction()`, `DB::commit()`, and `DB::rollback()` before commit. Rollback reverts writes performed in the transaction. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/interact-data/transactions.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5301b47f4679a9ef1b2cb0d014bc963851739867d95572f2f9294dab4da5e4a8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3f8105b03d02085e5af6315766089bc75364ce9c3fb0262df205ece0b23ea352",
            "ev:70638c7b191a277fbf0ea41bbbe7d2c62757eddefd4c71883a1ae75d1537a7b0",
            "ev:98cc39505c5027ec6d92b745f069d007c51012fc47eeb8b18f7f55f2c2cb2971"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://laravel.com/docs/12.x/database"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Standalone MongoDB deployments do not support these transactions. The Laravel MongoDB transaction guide prescribes a replica set or sharded cluster, rejects nested transactions with a `RuntimeException`, and disallows parallel operations inside a single transaction. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/interact-data/transactions.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:838b703590695d07fa0f73521b94130df5bad8282ea1a953c38e7311b52a82e2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:dd7a775da6fbaec703a242de7b65922d3eed3adb67df141841ff13a810f98fdd"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transaction guide states that Laravel MongoDB does not support `Illuminate\\Foundation\\Testing\\DatabaseTransactions` or `Illuminate\\Foundation\\Testing\\RefreshDatabase`; it suggests `Illuminate\\Foundation\\Testing\\DatabaseMigrations` to reset the database after each test. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/php/laravel-mongodb/current/interact-data/transactions.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d0c4789139863449932e8cd2c7942284d0da48a22e0df900efd4fc33fb4f0e2d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:f4e97e992fb5747f1c1f50ca0a340d38ccce09811a5e237017d90f63bafaffe2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Issue #2720 reported `firstOrCreate()` failing inside a transaction on Laravel MongoDB 4.1 with “Transaction already in progress”; the 4.2 release announcement says the issue was fixed by implementing `Model::createOrFirst()` with atomic `findOneAndUpdate`. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/mongodb/laravel-mongodb/issues/2720",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e25c8cd98b787c35eaef81a5d0feeeb46ec09066d830e60bb19b6cca02b0080b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
